uid\" content=\"34964109\" />\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_uid\" content=\"34964109\" />\n  \n\n\n\n  <!-- Social meta tags for unfurling urls -->\n  \n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"34964109\"><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,nofollow,noarchive\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"34964109\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34964109/?format=pubmed\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"34964109\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\"><meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"PubMed\"><meta name=\"twitter:domain\" content=\"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"34964109\"><meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34964109/?format=pubmed\"><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"34964109\"><meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\">\n\n\n  <!-- OpenSearch XML -->\n  <link rel=\"search\" type=\"application/opensearchdescription+xml\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/opensearch.xml\" title=\"PubMed search\">\n\n  <!-- Disables severely broken elements when no JS -->\n  <noscript>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/a2ffdabe-e220-486a-83d1-09afbe4369a3/core/no-script.css\">\n  </noscript>\n\n  \n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34964109/?format=pubmed\" />\n  \n\n\n</head>\n<body >\n\n  \n  <div class=\"article-page\" id=\"article-page\">\n    \n      <pre class=\"article-details\" id=\"article-details\">PMID- 34964109\r\nOWN - NLM\r\nSTAT- MEDLINE\r\nDCOM- 20220422\r\nLR  - 20230721\r\nIS  - 1399-0004 (Electronic)\r\nIS  - 0009-9163 (Print)\r\nIS  - 0009-9163 (Linking)\r\nVI  - 101\r\nIP  - 3\r\nDP  - 2022 Mar\r\nTI  - A splice site mutation in the TSEN2 causes a new syndrome with craniofacial and \r\n      central nervous system malformations, and atypical hemolytic uremic syndrome.\r\nPG  - 346-358\r\nLID - 10.1111/cge.14105 [doi]\r\nAB  - Recessive mutations in the genes encoding the four subunits of the tRNA splicing \r\n      endonuclease complex (TSEN54, TSEN34, TSEN15, and TSEN2) cause various forms of \r\n      pontocerebellar hypoplasia, a disorder characterized by hypoplasia of the \r\n      cerebellum and the pons, microcephaly, dysmorphisms, and other variable clinical \r\n      features. Here, we report an intronic recessive founder variant in the gene TSEN2 \r\n      that results in abnormal splicing of the mRNA of this gene, in six individuals \r\n      from four consanguineous families affected with microcephaly, multiple \r\n      craniofacial malformations, radiological abnormalities of the central nervous \r\n      system, and cognitive retardation of variable severity. Remarkably, unlike \r\n      patients with previously described mutations in the components of the TSEN \r\n      complex, all the individuals that we report developed atypical hemolytic uremic \r\n      syndrome (aHUS) with thrombotic microangiopathy, microangiopathic hemolytic \r\n      anemia, thrombocytopenia, proteinuria, severe hypertension, and end-stage kidney \r\n      disease (ESKD) early in life. Bulk RNA sequencing of peripheral blood cells of \r\n      four affected individuals revealed abnormal tRNA transcripts, indicating an \r\n      alteration of the tRNA biogenesis. Morpholino-mediated skipping of exon 10 of \r\n      tsen2 in zebrafish produced phenotypes similar to human patients. Thus, we have \r\n      identified a novel syndrome accompanied by aHUS suggesting the existence of a \r\n      link between tRNA biology and vascular endothelium homeostasis, which we propose \r\n      to name with the acronym TRACK syndrome (TSEN2 Related Atypical hemolytic uremic \r\n      syndrome, Craniofacial malformations, Kidney failure).\r\nCI  - © 2021 John Wiley &amp; Sons A/S . Published by John Wiley &amp; Sons Ltd.\r\nFAU - Canpolat, Nur\r\nAU  - Canpolat N\r\nAUID- ORCID: 0000-0002-3420-9756\r\nAD  - Department of Pediatric Nephrology, Istanbul University-Cerrahpasa, Cerrahpasa \r\n      Faculty of Medicine, Istanbul, Turkey.\r\nFAU - Liu, Dingxiao\r\nAU  - Liu D\r\nAUID- ORCID: 0000-0002-7581-2527\r\nAD  - Department of Internal Medicine, Carver College of Medicine, University of Iowa, \r\n      Iowa City, Iowa, USA.\r\nAD  - Department of Vascular Surgery, Second Xiangya Hospital, Central South \r\n      University, Changsha, Hunan, China.\r\nFAU - Atayar, Emine\r\nAU  - Atayar E\r\nAUID- ORCID: 0000-0001-8423-3431\r\nAD  - Nephrogenetics Laboratory, Department of Pediatric Nephrology, Hacettepe \r\n      University, Faculty of Medicine, Ankara, Turkey.\r\nFAU - Saygili, Seha\r\nAU  - Saygili S\r\nAUID- ORCID: 0000-0002-2424-6959\r\nAD  - Department of Pediatric Nephrology, Istanbul University-Cerrahpasa, Cerrahpasa \r\n      Faculty of Medicine, Istanbul, Turkey.\r\nFAU - Kara, Nazli Sila\r\nAU  - Kara NS\r\nAUID- ORCID: 0000-0002-6765-2543\r\nAD  - Biostatistics and Medical Informatics Program, Faculty of Medicine, Graduate \r\n      School of Health Sciences, Acibadem Mehmet Ali Aydinlar University, Istanbul, \r\n      Turkey.\r\nFAU - Westfall, Trudi A\r\nAU  - Westfall TA\r\nAD  - Department of Biology, University of Iowa, Iowa City, Iowa, USA.\r\nFAU - Ding, Qiong\r\nAU  - Ding Q\r\nAD  - Department of Internal Medicine, Carver College of Medicine, University of Iowa, \r\n      Iowa City, Iowa, USA.\r\nFAU - Brown, Bartley J\r\nAU  - Brown BJ\r\nAD  - Center for Bioinformatics and Computational Biology, University of Iowa, Iowa \r\n      City, Iowa, USA.\r\nFAU - Braun, Terry A\r\nAU  - Braun TA\r\nAD 